              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Knee-deep in Virginia’s New River with a fishing pole in hand, I finally found the Appalachian bliss I craved.</p><p><br></p><p>Not fifty yards up the bank, the heat of July came down like a weighted blanket. But there in the river bend, under black walnut groves, I felt as cool and content as all the trout that kept missing my bait.</p><p><br></p><p>After years in Seattle, I recently returned to the South, though not to the Atlanta metro where I was raised. Instead, I settled in the heart of Virginia’s Blue Ridge Mountains, which are both beautiful and, at this time of year, steamy. </p><p><br></p><p>They’ve reminded me just how hot a Southern summer can be.&nbsp;</p></div>
