          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>If you’re as pale as me, you may find your summer haven underground. Appalachia is home to countless cave systems that inspire marvel, wonder, and outerwear. Landmarks like Skyline Caverns in Virginia and Mammoth Cave National Park in Kentucky maintain temperatures in the fifties year-round, offering comfortable communion  with nature on hot and cold days alike. See some of our favorite Appalachian caves in “<a href="/blogs/outdoors-amp-travel/ready-to-escape-the-cold-try-caving">Ready to escape the cold? Try caving</a>.”</p><p><br></p><p>These ancient caverns serve as sanctuary to nature lovers no matter what extremities await outside. So dust off your winter coat when the temps hit the nineties and spelunk into the heart of the mountains.</p></div>
